We investigate a driven, open optical-lattice system featuring a scar-like state, where a Floquet-heating mechanism counteracts the dissipative cooling of the lattice potential. This dynamic equilibrium results in a Bose-Einstein condensation of bosons within the scar-like state. Furthermore, we demonstrate that this Floquet-heating-induced Bose condensation can be effectively controlled by adjusting the driving frequency. These findings offer a novel approach to generating Bose condensation in open optical-lattice systems. Additionally, the proposed Floquet-heating mechanism may hold significant potential for applications in quantum information processing. Finally, we anticipate that our results will inspire further research into Floquet-heating-induced Bose condensation. This study was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grant No. 11974280), the National Key R&D Program of China (Grant No. 2018YFA0306500), and the Fundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities (Grant No. 20720200010). Correspondence: yongqiang@hnu.edu.cn.
