Recent advancements in LiDAR-camera fusion have demonstrated that combining these sensors can significantly enhance 3D object detection. However, current methods often rely on complex, task-specific designs that are difficult to extend to other tasks. To address this, we introduce BEVFusion, a straightforward yet powerful fusion framework that leverages the complementary strengths of LiDAR and camera data. Our approach projects camera features into the bird's-eye view (BEV) space to align with LiDAR features, followed by a lightweight fusion module that integrates them. This design enables the fusion of features from any camera backbone with any LiDAR-based detector. Extensive experiments on the nuScenes dataset confirm that BEVFusion outperforms state-of-the-art methods, achieving a 2.0% improvement in AP over the second-best approach. Furthermore, BEVFusion is highly versatile, supporting various tasks including 3D detection, 3D tracking, and 3D semantic segmentation. The code and models are available at https://github.com/autonomousvision/bevfusion. The project's success is largely attributed to the community's enthusiastic contributions. We hope BEVFusion will serve as a solid foundation for future research. Please cite our paper if you find it useful.

